            <div xml:id="d255">

                <pb facs="0227" n="217" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg217"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3–3149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-31">March 31,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received March 31—6:37 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>685. Vernacular press March 26 reported Executive Yuan Council at first session
                    March 24 decided retain its Chiefs of Ministries and Political Vice Ministers in
                    Nanking, while retaining administrative units and Administrative Vice Ministers
                    in Canton.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 685; repeated Shanghai 315, Canton unnumbered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
